On 9/14/07, Alex Martini <alexjm@umich.edu> wrote:
>
> But {lu'o} isn't an article (a {gadri}) so you can't say {lu'o #
> broda} as far as I know.

You can, but only because {# broda} is a valid sumti,
a condensed form of {# lo broda}.

The # in {loi # broda} is an "inner quantifier", while the # in
{lu'o # broda} is an "outer quantifier".

That's as far as the syntax is concerned. The semantics of
{LAhE quantified-sumti} is problematic at least from a predicate
logic point of view.

